# Internationalization

Locales live under `resources/lang/{en,de}/`. User-facing copy must go through translations.

## Rules

- Do not hardcode UI strings in Blade, Livewire, controllers, validation messages, flashes, or emails.
- Use `__('file.key')`, `@lang`, or `trans()` with the existing file structure (e.g. `profile.php`, `validation.php`).
- When adding copy, update **both** `en` and `de` for the same key.
- Prefer extending an existing lang file over creating a new one unless the domain is clearly new.
- Validation messages belong in lang files / Form Request `messages()` that reference translation keys.

## Listing content translation (guide-written text)

- Automatic translation (`TranslateListingJob`, observers, page renders, scheduled tasks) must use the **free** Google
  engine (`FishingCopyGoogleTranslator`). Gemini is paid: only use it when someone runs it explicitly
  (`--engine=gemini`), never as a default.
- Skip the call when the stored content hash is unchanged, and cache detection results. The free endpoint answers 429
  when overused.
- `guidings.language` is the language the text is written in (can be `nl`, `en`, `de`, …), not the domain locale.
  Change it only via `GuidingTranslationService::changeSourceLanguage()`, which marks old translations stale.
- One `languages` row per (`source_id`, `type`, `language`). Don't add `title` or other columns to the
  `updateOrCreate` match.

```blade
{{-- ❌ BAD --}}
<button>Submit application</button>

{{-- ✅ GOOD --}}
<button>{{ __('profile.submit_application') }}</button>
```
